// CH1 - New Child Process of w3wp.exe - BYPASSED  |  Step 0 logic bug (+ ADE3-02)
// Rule intent : catch an IIS worker (w3wp.exe) spawning an unusual child process -
//               the classic "web shell spawned cmd/powershell/certutil" tell.
// The bug     : (1) LOGIC BUG - the rule can only ever see a *spawned child*. The
//               foothold compiles the implant IN-PROCESS with Roslyn and runs it via
//               Assembly.Load(bytes), so w3wp spawns NO child at all -> the attack is
//               invisible to this rule (it would have led straight to C2 on its own).
//               (2) ADE3-02 - the "child not seen in 14 days" baseline is poisonable:
//               one prior benign spawn of the same image name suppresses the alert.
// Try it      : on the CTF data this surfaces only the BENIGN w3wp -> csc.exe
//               compilation noise; the real foothold has no child, so it never appears.
SecurityEvent_CH1
| where ParentProcessName has "w3wp.exe"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, Account, NewProcessName, CommandLine, ParentProcessName